by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-03T17:10:54Z

Reworked to your lead @soyuka: `ObjectMapper.php` untouched, collection stays at container build.

Turns out there is nothing left to implement. `registerAttributeForAutoconfiguration(Map::class, ...)` already emits an `object_mapper.map` resource tag for every scanned class carrying the attribute, so `#[Map(source: NestedEntity::class)]` on the resource already puts `NestedEntity => NestedEntityResource` in the class map, and the nested property is filled. The functional test @Amoifr wrote fails on 8.2 only because the test app registers its fixtures one by one and the two resource classes were not among them. Adding them makes it pass with no source change. Standalone, `testClassMap` already covers the same shape through an explicit class map.

So the PR becomes tests: `ReverseMappingPass` had none, and the functional test now walks the whole chain.

My concern with the runtime version, for the record: it read `#[Map]` off the target property type at map time, which is the work you asked to keep out of the runtime, measured at +12% on mappings that do not use the feature and uncached. It also resolved only for nested values, so `map($category)` alone kept throwing, while the container path maps it. Two rules for the same attributes depending on whether there is a container seemed worse than the gap it closed.

The gap that remains is discoverability: a resource class excluded from the `App\` loader gets no tag and the nested mapping silently does not happen. Worth a docs note, maybe more.
